Best interview definition

"Docker uses a client-server architecture. The Docker Client sends commands through the Docker REST API to the Docker Daemon.
The Docker Daemon performs operations such as building images and creating and managing containers. Docker Registry is used to store and retrieve images."

Remember:

Client → API → Daemon → Containers
Registry → stores Docker images

